IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpc-dates`

-- Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA), s 41 and Schedule 3 (costs disclosure and adjudication) -- the rules a client of a
-- law practice meets about legal costs, centred on costs agreements: when the Schedule applies (cll 3-5), when costs
-- must be disclosed and what follows if they were not (cll 9, 11, 13, 18), interest (cl 23 with reg 61 of the Legal
-- Practitioners Regulations 2014), costs agreements (Part 5, cll 24-30 in full), bills (cll 31, 34), progress reports
-- (cl 19) and adjudication (cll 37, 44, 47, 49, 51). Seat-neutral: every rule is here, and the client's seat
-- (lpc-seat.l4) asks the questions. Three regulative rules (cl 31(1) with cl 34(4)-(5); cl 34(2); cl 37(4)) are run by
-- EVALTRACE inside functions that take only plain facts.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes or numbers. Where the text says no in its own words the outcome is a "no: ..." naming the
-- clause; where the clause does not reach the case the outcome says the clause "does not apply" (the 2026-11-04 and
-- 2026-11-05 rulings in substance). A court's or a principal's judgment ("satisfied", "fair and reasonable",
-- "significant", "reasonable grounds", "just and fair") is an input, never decided here.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act at version 1.9.2026, the
-- Legal Practitioners Regulations 2014 at version 1.7.2020; unauthorised RTF renderings). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Practitioners Act 1981, Schedule 3 -- the client's rules`

§§ `Dates the Act fixes`

-- Statutes Amendment (Legal Practitioners) Act 2013 (44/2013) s 61 inserted Schedule 3 from 1 July 2014; its Schedule
-- (transitional) cl 9(1): Schedule 3 applies to a matter in which the client first instructs the law practice on or
-- after that day. An earlier matter is outside this encoding (NOTES.md, scope).
`the day Schedule 3 commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 7 2014

§§ `Part 1 -- Interpretation (cl 1)`

-- cl 13(1)(c) lists the clients to whom costs need not be disclosed; reg 60 (under cl 13(1)(f)) adds a corporation
-- held for the Crown. Only (c) and (d) make a "sophisticated client" (cl 1).
DECLARE `Kind of client` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, or a business or body not listed below`
    `a law practice or a legal practitioner`
    `a public company, a subsidiary of a public company, a large proprietary company, a foreign company, a subsidiary of a foreign company or a registered Australian body`
    `a financial services licensee`
    `a liquidator, administrator or receiver`
    `a professional services partnership of more than 20 members, or one that would be a large proprietary company`
    `a joint venture company or group of the kind clause 13(1)(c)(vi) or (vii) describes`
    `a Minister, a government department or a public authority`
    `a corporation with share capital held mostly for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of client`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE k `is a client clause 13(1)(c) lists` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual, or a business or body not listed below` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation with share capital held mostly for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- cl 1: "sophisticated client means a client to whom, because of clause 13(1)(c) or (d), disclosure under clause 10 or
-- 11(1) is or was not required". cl 13(1)(d): the costs, or their basis, agreed as a result of a tender process.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of client`, `agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE k `with tender` `agreed by tender` `is a sophisticated client` IF
        k `is a client clause 13(1)(c) lists`
    OR  `agreed by tender`

§§ `Part 2 -- Application of the Schedule (cll 3, 4, 5; reg 58)`

DECLARE `Where first instructed` IS ONE OF
    `in South Australia`
    `in another Australian jurisdiction`
    `it cannot be determined where`

DECLARE `Application answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you first instructed the law practice in the matter in South Australia (cl 3)`
    `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`
    `no longer: the matter is connected with another jurisdiction and you chose that jurisdiction's costs law (cl 5)`
    `no: your notice was given more than 28 days after the law practice told you of your right to give it (cl 4(4))`
    `no: neither clause 3 nor clause 4 makes this Schedule apply to the matter`
    `not covered: you first instructed the law practice before Schedule 3 commenced on 1 July 2014`

-- cl 4(4): a notice "has no effect ... if it is given after the period of 28 days after the law practice discloses ...
-- the client's right": a notice on the 28th day counts (fork F7).
GIVEN `told of the right` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day told` IS A DATE, `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is too late (cl 4(4))` `told of the right` `the day told` `the day of the notice` IF
        `told of the right`
    AND `the days from` `the day told` `to` `the day of the notice` GREATER THAN 28

GIVEN `first instructed`                      IS A `Where first instructed`
      `the day first instructed`              IS A DATE
      `services mainly in South Australia`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `connected with South Australia`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `accepted an offer that it apply`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave written notice that it apply`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `told of the right`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day told`                          IS A DATE
      `the day of the notice`                 IS A DATE
      `connected with another jurisdiction`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `chose the other jurisdiction's law`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`does Schedule 3 apply (cll 3, 4, 5)` `first instructed` `the day first instructed` `services mainly in South Australia` `connected with South Australia` `accepted an offer that it apply` `gave written notice that it apply` `told of the right` `the day told` `the day of the notice` `connected with another jurisdiction` `chose the other jurisdiction's law` MEANS
    IF `the day first instructed` `is before` `the day Schedule 3 commenced`
    THEN `not covered: you first instructed the law practice before Schedule 3 commenced on 1 July 2014`
    ELSE IF (`applies by clause 3` OR `applies by clause 4`) AND `displaced by clause 5`
         THEN `no longer: the matter is connected with another jurisdiction and you chose that jurisdiction's costs law (cl 5)`
         ELSE IF `applies by clause 3`
              THEN `yes: you first instructed the law practice in the matter in South Australia (cl 3)`
              ELSE IF `applies by clause 4`
                   THEN `yes: you agreed with the law practice, or required it by written notice, that this Schedule apply, and the matter is connected with South Australia (cl 4)`
                   ELSE IF `open to clause 4` AND `gave written notice that it apply` AND `the notice is late`
                        THEN `no: your notice was given more than 28 days after the law practice told you of your right to give it (cl 4(4))`
                        ELSE `no: neither clause 3 nor clause 4 makes this Schedule apply to the matter`
    WHERE
        `applies by clause 3` MEANS
            CONSIDER `first instructed`
            WHEN `in South Australia` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        -- cl 4(1)(a), (b): the Schedule does not already apply (or the place cannot be determined), and the services
        -- are or will be provided wholly or primarily in this State, or the matter has a substantial connection with
        -- it (reg 58 lists when it has).
        `open to clause 4` MEANS
                (NOT `applies by clause 3`)
            AND (`services mainly in South Australia` OR `connected with South Australia`)
        `the notice is late` MEANS `the notice is too late (cl 4(4))` `told of the right` `the day told` `the day of the notice`
        `applies by clause 4` MEANS
                `open to clause 4`
            AND (`accepted an offer that it apply` OR (`gave written notice that it apply` AND (NOT `the notice is late`)))
        -- cl 5(2): services wholly or primarily in, or a substantial connection with, another jurisdiction, and the
        -- client agreed or notified (in time) under that jurisdiction's law.
        `displaced by clause 5` MEANS `connected with another jurisdiction` AND `chose the other jurisdiction's law`

§§ `Part 3 -- Costs disclosure (cll 9, 11, 13, 18)`

-- The "prescribed amount" of cl 13(1)(a) and (2): the deposited Regulations prescribe none, so $1 500 (exclusive of
-- GST) applies.
`the disclosure threshold (cl 13(1)(a))` MEANS 1500

DECLARE `Disclosure answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the law practice must disclose its costs to you in writing, before or as soon as practicable after it is retained (cll 10, 12)`
    `no: a barrister engaged for your matter need not disclose costs to you (cl 9)`
    `no: a law practice retained for you by your own law practice discloses to that law practice, which discloses to you (cl 11(2))`
    `no: the total legal costs, excluding disbursements, are not likely to exceed $1 500 excluding GST; if the law practice learns they are likely to, it must disclose as soon as practicable (cl 13(1)(a), (2))`
    `no: you had a disclosure in the previous 12 months and waived further disclosure in writing, and a principal decided on reasonable grounds that it was not warranted (cl 13(1)(b))`
    `no: you are a client of a kind clause 13(1)(c) lists, a sophisticated client (cl 13(1)(c))`
    `no: the costs or their basis were agreed through a tender process (cl 13(1)(d))`
    `no: you will not be required to pay the costs, and they will not otherwise be recovered (cl 13(1)(e))`
    `no: you are a corporation held for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory (cl 13(1)(f), reg 60)`

GIVEN `a barrister engaged for the matter`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `retained by another law practice for you`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the likely total legal costs`               IS A NUMBER
      `waived after a disclosure within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a principal decided further disclosure was not warranted` IS A BOOLEAN
      k                                            IS A `Kind of client`
      `agreed by tender`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `you will not be required to pay`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disclosure answer`
`must the law practice disclose its costs (cll 9-13)` `a barrister engaged for the matter` `retained by another law practice for you` `the likely total legal costs` `waived after a disclosure within 12 months` `a principal decided further disclosure was not warranted` k `agreed by tender` `you will not be required to pay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a barrister engaged for the matter`
            THEN `no: a barrister engaged for your matter need not disclose costs to you (cl 9)`
        IF `retained by another law practice for you`
            THEN `no: a law practice retained for you by your own law practice discloses to that law practice, which discloses to you (cl 11(2))`
        IF `the likely total legal costs` AT MOST `the disclosure threshold (cl 13(1)(a))`
            THEN `no: the total legal costs, excluding disbursements, are not likely to exceed $1 500 excluding GST; if the law practice learns they are likely to, it must disclose as soon as practicable (cl 13(1)(a), (2))`
        IF `waived after a disclosure within 12 months` AND `a principal decided further disclosure was not warranted`
            THEN `no: you had a disclosure in the previous 12 months and waived further disclosure in writing, and a principal decided on reasonable grounds that it was not warranted (cl 13(1)(b))`
        IF k `is a client clause 13(1)(c) lists`
            THEN `no: you are a client of a kind clause 13(1)(c) lists, a sophisticated client (cl 13(1)(c))`
        IF `agreed by tender`
            THEN `no: the costs or their basis were agreed through a tender process (cl 13(1)(d))`
        IF `you will not be required to pay`
            THEN `no: you will not be required to pay the costs, and they will not otherwise be recovered (cl 13(1)(e))`
        IF k EQUALS `a corporation with share capital held mostly for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
            THEN `no: you are a corporation held for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory (cl 13(1)(f), reg 60)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the law practice must disclose its costs to you in writing, before or as soon as practicable after it is retained (cll 10, 12)`

DECLARE `Failure to disclose answer` IS ONE OF
    `clause 18 does not apply: the law practice disclosed everything Part 3 required`
    `clause 18(1)-(4) do not apply to this law practice's own costs: it failed to disclose only because the law practice it retained for you did not give it the information (cl 18(5)(a))`
    `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; you may apply to set aside your costs agreement; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1)-(4))`
    `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1), (2), (4))`
    `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount; you may still apply to set aside your costs agreement (cl 18(1)-(3))`
    `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount (cl 18(1), (2))`

GIVEN `the law practice failed to disclose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `only because the retained law practice did not inform it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you entered a costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs have been adjudicated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Failure to disclose answer`
`what follows from a failure to disclose (cl 18)` `the law practice failed to disclose` `only because the retained law practice did not inform it` `you entered a costs agreement` `the costs have been adjudicated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the law practice failed to disclose`
            THEN `clause 18 does not apply: the law practice disclosed everything Part 3 required`
        IF `only because the retained law practice did not inform it`
            THEN `clause 18(1)-(4) do not apply to this law practice's own costs: it failed to disclose only because the law practice it retained for you did not give it the information (cl 18(5)(a))`
        IF `the costs have been adjudicated` AND `you entered a costs agreement`
            THEN `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount; you may still apply to set aside your costs agreement (cl 18(1)-(3))`
        IF `the costs have been adjudicated`
            THEN `the costs have been adjudicated, so you must pay the adjudicated amount (cl 18(1), (2))`
        IF `you entered a costs agreement`
            THEN `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; you may apply to set aside your costs agreement; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1)-(4))`
        OTHERWISE `you need not pay until the costs are adjudicated; the law practice cannot sue you for them until then; on adjudication the costs may be reduced (cl 18(1), (2), (4))`

§§ `Part 3 -- Progress reports (cl 19)`

DECLARE `Kind of report` IS ONE OF
    `a written report of the progress of the matter`
    `a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill`

DECLARE `Report charge answer` IS ONE OF
    `the law practice must give it on reasonable request, and may charge you a reasonable amount for it (cl 19(1)(a), (2))`
    `no: the law practice must give it on reasonable request and must not charge you for it (cl 19(1)(b), (2))`

GIVEN r IS A `Kind of report`
GIVETH A `Report charge answer`
`may the law practice charge for the report (cl 19)` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `a written report of the progress of the matter` THEN `the law practice must give it on reasonable request, and may charge you a reasonable amount for it (cl 19(1)(a), (2))`
    OTHERWISE `no: the law practice must give it on reasonable request and must not charge you for it (cl 19(1)(b), (2))`

§§ `Part 4 -- Interest on unpaid legal costs (cl 23; reg 61)`

-- reg 61(2): "the Cash Rate Target as at the relevant date, increased by 2 percentage points"; reg 61(3): the relevant
-- date is the date the bill was issued. The Cash Rate Target is an input (a Reserve Bank figure, not deposited).
GIVEN `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest interest rate (cl 23(4), reg 61)` `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill` MEANS
    `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill` PLUS 2

DECLARE `Interest answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the bill does not state that interest is payable and the rate (cl 23(3))`
    `no: the rate is above the most the regulations allow, the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill plus 2 percentage points (cl 23(4), reg 61)`
    `yes: your costs agreement provides for interest (cl 23(2))`
    `yes: the costs have been unpaid for 30 days or more after the bill (cl 23(1))`
    `not yet: interest may be charged only once the costs are unpaid 30 days or more after the bill, unless your costs agreement provides for it (cl 23(1), (2))`

-- cl 23(1) "unpaid 30 days or more after the practice has given a bill": the 30th day after the bill counts (fork F4).
GIVEN `the bill states interest and its rate`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the bill`                    IS A DATE
      `the day interest would run from`        IS A DATE
      `the rate charged`                       IS A NUMBER
      `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Interest answer`
`may the law practice charge interest (cl 23)` `the bill states interest and its rate` `the costs agreement provides for interest` `the day of the bill` `the day interest would run from` `the rate charged` `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bill states interest and its rate`
            THEN `no: the bill does not state that interest is payable and the rate (cl 23(3))`
        IF `the rate charged` GREATER THAN `the highest interest rate (cl 23(4), reg 61)` `the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill`
            THEN `no: the rate is above the most the regulations allow, the Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill plus 2 percentage points (cl 23(4), reg 61)`
        IF `the costs agreement provides for interest`
            THEN `yes: your costs agreement provides for interest (cl 23(2))`
        IF `the days from` `the day of the bill` `to` `the day interest would run from` AT LEAST 30
            THEN `yes: the costs have been unpaid for 30 days or more after the bill (cl 23(1))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet: interest may be charged only once the costs are unpaid 30 days or more after the bill, unless your costs agreement provides for it (cl 23(1), (2))`

§§ `Part 5 -- Costs agreements (cll 24-30)`

§§§ `The parties and the matter`

-- cl 24(1). (d) with cl 24(6) and reg 62: for an agreement with an associated third party payer to which the client is
-- not a party, clause 25 reads "client" as that payer, so the payer stands where the client stands.
DECLARE `Parties to the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `you and the law practice you retained`
    `you and a law practice your law practice retained for you`
    `your law practice and a law practice it retained for you`
    `the law practice and an associated third party payer (someone who owes the law practice your costs)`

-- cl 25(2) and cl 26(1a). cl 25(2)(c)(ii) was deleted by Act 70/2017 from 1 March 2018 (finding 1); cl 25(2)(d):
-- the deposited Regulations prescribe no further kind of matter.
DECLARE `Kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `a criminal matter`
    `a matter that relates to or involves child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption`
    `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 of the Commonwealth`
    `proceedings under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 of the Commonwealth`
    `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth`
    `another matter, for example a personal injury, compensation or other civil claim`

GIVEN m IS A `Kind of matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE m `is excluded from conditional costs agreements (cl 25(2))` IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another matter, for example a personal injury, compensation or other civil claim` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Conditional matter answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a conditional (no win, no fee) costs agreement may relate to this matter (cl 25(1), (2))`
    `yes, but without an uplift fee: a conditional costs agreement may relate to this matter, but not provide for an uplift fee (cll 25(2), 26(1a))`
    `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a criminal matter (cl 25(2)(a))`
    `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter involving child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption (cl 25(2)(b))`
    `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (cl 25(2)(c))`

GIVEN m IS A `Kind of matter`
GIVETH A `Conditional matter answer`
`may the agreement be conditional for this matter (cl 25(2))` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a criminal matter` THEN `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a criminal matter (cl 25(2)(a))`
    WHEN `a matter that relates to or involves child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption` THEN `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter involving child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption (cl 25(2)(b))`
    WHEN `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 of the Commonwealth` THEN `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (cl 25(2)(c))`
    WHEN `proceedings under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 of the Commonwealth` THEN `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (cl 25(2)(c))`
    WHEN `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth` THEN `yes, but without an uplift fee: a conditional costs agreement may relate to this matter, but not provide for an uplift fee (cll 25(2), 26(1a))`
    OTHERWISE `yes: a conditional (no win, no fee) costs agreement may relate to this matter (cl 25(1), (2))`

§§§ `Uplift fees (cl 26)`

-- cl 1: an uplift fee is additional legal costs (excluding disbursements) payable on the successful outcome.
-- cl 26(4)(b): "must not exceed 25% of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable" -- the base is the
-- costs without the uplift and without disbursements; exactly 25% is allowed (fork F9).
GIVEN `the legal costs otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most uplift fee in a litigious matter (cl 26(4)(b))` `the legal costs otherwise payable` MEANS
    `the legal costs otherwise payable` TIMES 0.25

DECLARE `Uplift answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: an uplift fee may be provided for only in a conditional costs agreement (cll 1, 26(1))`
    `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter at all (cl 25(2))`
    `no: not in a conditional costs agreement for proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 (cl 26(1a))`
    `no: in a litigious matter, only if the risk of the claim failing, and of your having to meet your own costs, is significant (cl 26(4)(a))`
    `yes: at most 25% of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable (cl 26(4)(b))`
    `yes: Schedule 3 sets no maximum for a matter that is not litigious; the agreement must still identify the basis and estimate the fee (cl 26(2), (3))`

GIVEN `the agreement is conditional` IS A BOOLEAN
      m IS A `Kind of matter`
      `the matter is litigious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk is significant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Uplift answer`
`may the agreement provide for an uplift fee (cl 26)` `the agreement is conditional` m `the matter is litigious` `the risk is significant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the agreement is conditional`
            THEN `no: an uplift fee may be provided for only in a conditional costs agreement (cll 1, 26(1))`
        IF m `is excluded from conditional costs agreements (cl 25(2))`
            THEN `no: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter at all (cl 25(2))`
        IF m EQUALS `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth`
            THEN `no: not in a conditional costs agreement for proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 (cl 26(1a))`
        IF `the matter is litigious` AND (NOT `the risk is significant`)
            THEN `no: in a litigious matter, only if the risk of the claim failing, and of your having to meet your own costs, is significant (cl 26(4)(a))`
        IF `the matter is litigious`
            THEN `yes: at most 25% of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable (cl 26(4)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: Schedule 3 sets no maximum for a matter that is not litigious; the agreement must still identify the basis and estimate the fee (cl 26(2), (3))`

§§§ `Contingency fees (cl 27)`

DECLARE `Contingency answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: a costs agreement may not calculate what you pay by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered; such an agreement is void and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter (cll 27(1), 29(1), (5))`
    `allowed to the extent that the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs (cl 27(2))`
    `clause 27 does not apply: what you pay is not calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or property recovered`

GIVEN `calculated by reference to the award` IS A BOOLEAN, `it adopts an applicable scale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contingency answer`
`is the fee a prohibited contingency fee (cl 27)` `calculated by reference to the award` `it adopts an applicable scale` MEANS
    IF NOT `calculated by reference to the award`
    THEN `clause 27 does not apply: what you pay is not calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or property recovered`
    ELSE IF `it adopts an applicable scale`
         THEN `allowed to the extent that the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs (cl 27(2))`
         ELSE `no: a costs agreement may not calculate what you pay by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered; such an agreement is void and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter (cll 27(1), 29(1), (5))`

§§§ `Is the costs agreement valid (cll 24-27, 29(1), 51)`

-- One costs agreement, as the client can describe it. A field no clause reads in a given case is still asked: the
-- seat supplies it.
DECLARE `Costs agreement` HAS
    `parties`                                IS A `Parties to the agreement`
    `in writing or evidenced in writing`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `accepted by conduct`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offer states what clause 24(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excludes adjudication`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `conditional`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `matter`                                 IS A `Kind of matter`
    `sets out the successful outcome`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `in clear plain language`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the client`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the right to independent advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooling-off business days`              IS A NUMBER
    `has an uplift fee`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift basis separately identified`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift estimated`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `litigious`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `risk significant`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift fee`                             IS A NUMBER
    `costs otherwise payable`                IS A NUMBER
    `contingency`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `adopts a scale`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `client is sophisticated`                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Validity answer` IS ONE OF
    `void: it is not in writing or evidenced in writing (cll 24(2), 29(1))`
    `void: it was accepted by conduct, but the offer did not clearly state that it was an offer to enter a costs agreement, that it could be accepted in writing or by conduct, and what conduct would accept it (cll 24(3), (4), 29(1))`
    `void: it says the costs are not subject to adjudication, and you are not a sophisticated client who may contract out (cll 24(5), 29(1), 51)`
    `void: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter (cll 25(2), 29(1))`
    `void: a conditional costs agreement may not be accepted by conduct; it must be in writing (cll 24(3) note, 25(3)(c)(i), 29(1))`
    `void: it does not set out the circumstances that are the successful outcome (cll 25(3)(a), 29(1))`
    `void: it is not in clear plain language (cll 25(3)(c)(ii), 29(1))`
    `void: it is not signed by you (cll 25(3)(c)(iii), 29(1))`
    `void: it does not state that you were told of your right to independent legal advice (cll 25(3)(d), 29(1))`
    `void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
    `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
    `void, and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter: it is a contingency fee agreement (cll 27, 29(1), (5))`
    `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `is relieved of the signing, advice and cooling-off rules (cl 25(4), (5))` IF
        a's `client is sophisticated`
    OR  a's `parties` EQUALS `your law practice and a law practice it retained for you`

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `breaches clause 26` IF
        a's `conditional`
    AND a's `has an uplift fee`
    AND (    a's `matter` EQUALS `proceedings under the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth`
         OR  (NOT a's `uplift basis separately identified`)
         OR  (NOT a's `uplift estimated`)
         OR  (a's `litigious` AND (NOT a's `risk significant`))
         OR  (a's `litigious` AND a's `uplift fee` GREATER THAN `the most uplift fee in a litigious matter (cl 26(4)(b))` (a's `costs otherwise payable`)))

-- An uplift fee in an agreement that is not conditional is not an "uplift fee" (cl 1 ties it to the successful
-- outcome), so clause 26 is not reached; such an agreement is tested by the other rules only (fork F10).
-- Order of the answers: the most serious consequence first (cl 29(5), then cl 29(4)), then the clauses in order.
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement`
GIVETH A `Validity answer`
`is the costs agreement void (cll 24-27, 29)` a MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a's `contingency` AND (NOT a's `adopts a scale`)
            THEN `void, and the law practice can recover nothing for its services in the matter: it is a contingency fee agreement (cll 27, 29(1), (5))`
        IF a `breaches clause 26`
            THEN `void, and the law practice can recover no uplift fee: it provides for an uplift fee that clause 26 does not allow (cll 26, 29(1), (4))`
        IF NOT a's `in writing or evidenced in writing`
            THEN `void: it is not in writing or evidenced in writing (cll 24(2), 29(1))`
        IF a's `accepted by conduct` AND a's `conditional`
            THEN `void: a conditional costs agreement may not be accepted by conduct; it must be in writing (cll 24(3) note, 25(3)(c)(i), 29(1))`
        IF a's `accepted by conduct` AND (NOT a's `the offer states what clause 24(4) requires`)
            THEN `void: it was accepted by conduct, but the offer did not clearly state that it was an offer to enter a costs agreement, that it could be accepted in writing or by conduct, and what conduct would accept it (cll 24(3), (4), 29(1))`
        IF a's `excludes adjudication` AND (NOT a's `client is sophisticated`)
            THEN `void: it says the costs are not subject to adjudication, and you are not a sophisticated client who may contract out (cll 24(5), 29(1), 51)`
        IF a's `conditional` AND (a's `matter`) `is excluded from conditional costs agreements (cl 25(2))`
            THEN `void: a conditional costs agreement may not relate to this kind of matter (cll 25(2), 29(1))`
        IF a's `conditional` AND (NOT a's `sets out the successful outcome`)
            THEN `void: it does not set out the circumstances that are the successful outcome (cll 25(3)(a), 29(1))`
        IF a's `conditional` AND (NOT a's `in clear plain language`)
            THEN `void: it is not in clear plain language (cll 25(3)(c)(ii), 29(1))`
        IF a's `conditional` AND (NOT a's `signed by the client`) AND (NOT a `is relieved of the signing, advice and cooling-off rules (cl 25(4), (5))`)
            THEN `void: it is not signed by you (cll 25(3)(c)(iii), 29(1))`
        IF a's `conditional` AND (NOT a's `states the right to independent advice`) AND (NOT a `is relieved of the signing, advice and cooling-off rules (cl 25(4), (5))`)
            THEN `void: it does not state that you were told of your right to independent legal advice (cll 25(3)(d), 29(1))`
        IF a's `conditional` AND a's `cooling-off business days` LESS THAN 5 AND (NOT a `is relieved of the signing, advice and cooling-off rules (cl 25(4), (5))`)
            THEN `void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
        OTHERWISE `not void under Part 5: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Parts 5 and 7 (cl 28)`

§§§ `Cooling off (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`

DECLARE `Cooling-off answer` IS ONE OF
    `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: the agreement is not a conditional costs agreement`
    `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: you are a sophisticated client, or the agreement is between two law practices (cl 25(4), (5))`
    `the agreement is void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
    `yes: you may end it by written notice now; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before you ended it on your instructions and knowing it would be done in the cooling-off period, and no uplift fee (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`
    `no: the cooling-off period has ended`

-- Fork F6: "a cooling-off period of not less than 5 clear business days": the period is counted in business days
-- (cl 1: not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday) beginning the business day after the day the agreement was made.
-- The client gives the count, so public holidays need no calendar here. Today falls in the period if the business days
-- from the first one up to today (today counted if it is a business day) are no more than the period's length.
GIVEN `the agreement is conditional`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `relieved of the cooling-off rule`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period in the agreement`                 IS A NUMBER
      `business days since the agreement was made`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cooling-off answer`
`may I end the agreement in the cooling-off period (cl 25)` `the agreement is conditional` `relieved of the cooling-off rule` `the period in the agreement` `business days since the agreement was made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the agreement is conditional`
            THEN `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: the agreement is not a conditional costs agreement`
        IF `relieved of the cooling-off rule`
            THEN `clause 25 gives no cooling-off period: you are a sophisticated client, or the agreement is between two law practices (cl 25(4), (5))`
        IF `the period in the agreement` LESS THAN 5
            THEN `the agreement is void: it does not give a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days (cll 25(3)(e), 29(1))`
        IF `business days since the agreement was made` AT MOST `the period in the agreement`
            THEN `yes: you may end it by written notice now; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before you ended it on your instructions and knowing it would be done in the cooling-off period, and no uplift fee (cl 25(3)(e), (6))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the cooling-off period has ended`

§§§ `What a void agreement leaves the law practice (cl 29(2)-(6))`

DECLARE `Why the agreement is void` IS ONE OF
    `it is a contingency fee agreement (cl 27)`
    `it breaches clause 26 (uplift fees)`
    `it breaches another provision of Part 5`

-- cl 29(2): costs under a void agreement are recoverable under cl 21(b) (scale) or (c) (fair and reasonable value): an
-- input, settled by agreement or adjudication. cl 29(3): never more than the agreement would have given. cl 29(4): no
-- part of the uplift fee where cl 26 is breached. cl 29(5): nothing where cl 27 is breached.
GIVEN `why`                                   IS A `Why the agreement is void`
      `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement amount without uplift`   IS A NUMBER
      `the uplift fee`                        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the law practice may recover under a void agreement (cl 29)` `why` `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` `the agreement amount without uplift` `the uplift fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `it is a contingency fee agreement (cl 27)` THEN 0
    WHEN `it breaches clause 26 (uplift fees)` THEN `the smaller of` `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` `and` `the agreement amount without uplift`
    OTHERWISE `the smaller of` `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` `and` (`the agreement amount without uplift` PLUS `the uplift fee`)

-- cl 29(3)-(5) "must repay"; cl 29(6): recoverable as a debt.
GIVEN `why`                                   IS A `Why the agreement is void`
      `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement amount without uplift`   IS A NUMBER
      `the uplift fee`                        IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid`                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount to be repaid under a void agreement (cl 29)` `why` `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` `the agreement amount without uplift` `the uplift fee` `the amount paid` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 `and` (`the amount paid` MINUS `the most the law practice may recover under a void agreement (cl 29)` `why` `the scale or fair and reasonable amount` `the agreement amount without uplift` `the uplift fee`)

§§§ `Setting aside a costs agreement (cl 30)`

DECLARE `Set aside answer` IS ONE OF
    `you may apply to the Supreme Court; it may set the agreement aside only if satisfied that it is not fair and reasonable (cl 30(1))`
    `the Supreme Court may set it aside, and then order what you pay: the applicable scale, or fair and reasonable costs, never more than the agreement would have given (cl 30(1), (4)-(6))`

GIVEN `the court is satisfied it is not fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
`can the costs agreement be set aside (cl 30)` `the court is satisfied it is not fair and reasonable` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied it is not fair and reasonable`
    THEN `the Supreme Court may set it aside, and then order what you pay: the applicable scale, or fair and reasonable costs, never more than the agreement would have given (cl 30(1), (4)-(6))`
    ELSE `you may apply to the Supreme Court; it may set the agreement aside only if satisfied that it is not fair and reasonable (cl 30(1))`

-- cl 30(6).
GIVEN `the court's figure` IS A NUMBER, `the agreement amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the court may order after setting aside (cl 30(6))` `the court's figure` `the agreement amount` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `the court's figure` `and` `the agreement amount`

§§ `Part 6 -- Billing (cll 31, 34): two regulative rules`

DECLARE `Costs party` IS ONE OF `the law practice`, `the client`

DECLARE `Costs act` IS ONE OF
    `commence proceedings to recover the legal costs`
    `give the itemised bill`
    `apply for adjudication of the costs`

-- cl 31(1): "must not commence legal proceedings to recover legal costs ... until at least 30 days after the law
-- practice has given a bill"; cl 34(4)-(5) the same 30 days from a lump sum bill or from complying with a request for
-- an itemised bill. Clock: day 0 is the day the bill (or the itemised bill) was given. Fork F2: proceedings on the
-- 30th day after are "at least 30 days after", so the bar covers days 0 to 29 (WITHIN is inclusive on the stable l4).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`cl 31(1) -- the law practice must not sue for its costs until at least 30 days after the bill` MEANS
    PARTY  `the law practice`
    SHANT  `commence proceedings to recover the legal costs`
    WITHIN 29
    LEST   BREACH BY `the law practice` BECAUSE "cl 31(1), 34(4)-(5): proceedings commenced less than 30 days after the bill; the court must stay them (cl 31(3))"

-- cl 34(2): "must comply with the request within 21 days after the date on which the request is made". Clock: day 0 is
-- the day of the request; day 21 is in time (fork F3).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`cl 34(2) -- the law practice must give the itemised bill within 21 days after the request` MEANS
    PARTY  `the law practice`
    MUST   `give the itemised bill`
    WITHIN 21
    LEST   BREACH BY `the law practice` BECAUSE "cl 34(2): the itemised bill was not given within 21 days after the request"

-- cl 37(4): an application by a client "must be made within 6 months after" the bill or request for payment (or the
-- payment). Clock: day 0 is that day.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`cl 37(4) -- the client must apply for adjudication within 6 months` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the client`
    MUST   `apply for adjudication of the costs`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the client` BECAUSE "cl 37(4): the application was not made within 6 months; only the court's leave under cl 37(5) remains"

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so FULFILLED is matched and
-- everything else is the other answer. These helpers take a DEONTIC value, so they are never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`, `who` IS A `Costs party`, `the act` IS A `Costs act`, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule` `is kept when` `who` `does` `the act` `on day` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `who` `the act` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Proceedings answer` IS ONE OF
    `not until the costs have been adjudicated: the law practice failed to make a disclosure Part 3 required (cl 18(2))`
    `not until the adjudication you applied for has been completed (cl 44(c))`
    `not until it has given you a bill in accordance with clauses 32 and 33, and 30 days have passed (cl 31(1))`
    `not until it has given you the itemised bill you asked for, and 30 days have passed (cl 34(5))`
    `yes: the court authorised earlier proceedings because you are about to leave the State (cl 31(2))`
    `yes: at least 30 days have passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))`
    `not yet: 30 days have not passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5)); a court must stay proceedings brought now (cl 31(3))`

-- The day the 30 days run from: the itemised bill, where one was asked for and given; otherwise the bill.
GIVEN `the day of the bill` IS A DATE, `asked for an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the itemised bill was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the 30 days run from (cll 31(1), 34(5))` `the day of the bill` `asked for an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was given` MEANS
    IF `asked for an itemised bill` THEN `the day the itemised bill was given` ELSE `the day of the bill`

GIVEN `the day of the bill` IS A DATE, `asked for an itemised bill` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the itemised bill was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day the law practice may sue (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))` `the day of the bill` `asked for an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was given` MEANS
    (`the day the 30 days run from (cll 31(1), 34(5))` `the day of the bill` `asked for an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was given`) `plus days` 30

GIVEN `failed to disclose and not yet adjudicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adjudication is pending`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bill was given`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the bill`                        IS A DATE
      `asked for an itemised bill`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the itemised bill was given`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the itemised bill was given`        IS A DATE
      `the court authorised earlier proceedings`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the proceedings`                 IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Proceedings answer`
`may the law practice sue for its costs (cll 18(2), 31, 34, 44)` `failed to disclose and not yet adjudicated` `an adjudication is pending` `a bill was given` `the day of the bill` `asked for an itemised bill` `the itemised bill was given` `the day the itemised bill was given` `the court authorised earlier proceedings` `the day of the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `failed to disclose and not yet adjudicated`
            THEN `not until the costs have been adjudicated: the law practice failed to make a disclosure Part 3 required (cl 18(2))`
        IF `an adjudication is pending`
            THEN `not until the adjudication you applied for has been completed (cl 44(c))`
        IF NOT `a bill was given`
            THEN `not until it has given you a bill in accordance with clauses 32 and 33, and 30 days have passed (cl 31(1))`
        IF `asked for an itemised bill` AND (NOT `the itemised bill was given`)
            THEN `not until it has given you the itemised bill you asked for, and 30 days have passed (cl 34(5))`
        IF `the court authorised earlier proceedings`
            THEN `yes: the court authorised earlier proceedings because you are about to leave the State (cl 31(2))`
        IF `cl 31(1) -- the law practice must not sue for its costs until at least 30 days after the bill` `is kept when` `the law practice` `does` `commence proceedings to recover the legal costs` `on day` (`the days from` (`the day the 30 days run from (cll 31(1), 34(5))` `the day of the bill` `asked for an itemised bill` `the day the itemised bill was given`) `to` `the day of the proceedings`)
            THEN `yes: at least 30 days have passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet: 30 days have not passed since the bill (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5)); a court must stay proceedings brought now (cl 31(3))`

GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the itemised bill (cl 34(2))` `the day of the request` MEANS `the day of the request` `plus days` 21

DECLARE `Itemised bill answer` IS ONE OF
    `clause 34 does not apply: an itemised bill may be requested only after a bill that is not itemised (cl 34(1))`
    `in time: it was given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
    `late: it was not given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
    `still in time: the 21 days after your request have not yet run out (cl 34(2))`

GIVEN `the bill was not itemised`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the request`           IS A DATE
      `it has been given`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was given`             IS A DATE
      `today`                            IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Itemised bill answer`
`was the itemised bill given in time (cl 34)` `the bill was not itemised` `the day of the request` `it has been given` `the day it was given` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `the bill was not itemised`
    THEN `clause 34 does not apply: an itemised bill may be requested only after a bill that is not itemised (cl 34(1))`
    ELSE IF `it has been given`
         THEN IF `kept on` `the day it was given`
              THEN `in time: it was given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
              ELSE `late: it was not given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
         ELSE IF `kept on` `today`
              THEN `still in time: the 21 days after your request have not yet run out (cl 34(2))`
              ELSE `late: it was not given within 21 days after your request (cl 34(2))`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        DECIDE `kept on` `the day` IF
            `cl 34(2) -- the law practice must give the itemised bill within 21 days after the request` `is kept when` `the law practice` `does` `give the itemised bill` `on day` (`the days from` `the day of the request` `to` `the day`)

§§ `Part 7 -- Adjudication of costs (cll 37, 44, 47, 49, 51)`

-- cl 37(4): within 6 months after (a) the bill was given or the request for payment made, or (b) the costs were paid
-- if there was neither. The client states the day that applies. Fork F1 for the months.
GIVEN `the day the 6 months run from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for adjudication (cl 37(4))` `the day the 6 months run from` MEANS
    `the day the 6 months run from` `plus months` 6

DECLARE `Adjudication time answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: as a sophisticated client you contracted out of Part 7 (cl 51)`
    `in time: the application was made within 6 months (cl 37(4))`
    `still in time: the 6 months have not yet run out (cl 37(4))`
    `out of time, but the Supreme Court may deal with it if, having regard to the delay and the reasons for it, it decides that is just and fair (cl 37(5))`
    `out of time, and the Supreme Court has decided it is just and fair to deal with it (cl 37(5))`
    `out of time, and as a sophisticated client you cannot ask the court to deal with it late (cl 37(5)(a))`

GIVEN `sophisticated`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `contracted out`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the 6 months run from` IS A DATE
      `applied`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day applied`              IS A DATE
      `today`                        IS A DATE
      `the court found it just and fair` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Adjudication time answer`
`can the application for adjudication be dealt with (cll 37, 51)` `sophisticated` `contracted out` `the day the 6 months run from` `applied` `the day applied` `today` `the court found it just and fair` MEANS
    IF `sophisticated` AND `contracted out`
    THEN `no: as a sophisticated client you contracted out of Part 7 (cl 51)`
    ELSE IF `in time on` (IF `applied` THEN `the day applied` ELSE `today`)
         THEN IF `applied`
              THEN `in time: the application was made within 6 months (cl 37(4))`
              ELSE `still in time: the 6 months have not yet run out (cl 37(4))`
         ELSE IF `sophisticated`
              THEN `out of time, and as a sophisticated client you cannot ask the court to deal with it late (cl 37(5)(a))`
              ELSE IF `the court found it just and fair`
                   THEN `out of time, and the Supreme Court has decided it is just and fair to deal with it (cl 37(5))`
                   ELSE `out of time, but the Supreme Court may deal with it if, having regard to the delay and the reasons for it, it decides that is just and fair (cl 37(5))`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day the 6 months run from` `to` (`the last day to apply for adjudication (cl 37(4))` `the day the 6 months run from`)
        `the rule for this application` MEANS `cl 37(4) -- the client must apply for adjudication within 6 months` `the days allowed`
        GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        DECIDE `in time on` `the day` IF
            `the rule for this application` `is kept when` `the client` `does` `apply for adjudication of the costs` `on day` (`the days from` `the day the 6 months run from` `to` `the day`)

DECLARE `Agreement measure answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court must adjudicate the disputed costs by the terms of your costs agreement (cl 47(1))`
    `no: the agreement does not specify the amount, or a rate or other means of calculating it, for these costs (cl 47(1)(a))`
    `no: the agreement has been set aside (cll 30, 47(1)(b))`
    `no: the court is satisfied that the agreement does not comply in a material respect with the disclosure requirements of Part 3 (cl 47(1)(c))`
    `no: the court is satisfied that Part 5 stops the law practice recovering these costs (cl 47(1)(d))`
    `no: you and the law practice agreed otherwise (cl 47(1)(e))`

GIVEN `it specifies the amount or a rate`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was set aside`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds a material disclosure failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds Part 5 precludes recovery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties agreed otherwise`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Agreement measure answer`
`is the adjudication by the costs agreement (cl 47)` `it specifies the amount or a rate` `it was set aside` `the court finds a material disclosure failure` `the court finds Part 5 precludes recovery` `the parties agreed otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it specifies the amount or a rate`
            THEN `no: the agreement does not specify the amount, or a rate or other means of calculating it, for these costs (cl 47(1)(a))`
        IF `it was set aside`
            THEN `no: the agreement has been set aside (cll 30, 47(1)(b))`
        IF `the court finds a material disclosure failure`
            THEN `no: the court is satisfied that the agreement does not comply in a material respect with the disclosure requirements of Part 3 (cl 47(1)(c))`
        IF `the court finds Part 5 precludes recovery`
            THEN `no: the court is satisfied that Part 5 stops the law practice recovering these costs (cl 47(1)(d))`
        IF `the parties agreed otherwise`
            THEN `no: you and the law practice agreed otherwise (cl 47(1)(e))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the court must adjudicate the disputed costs by the terms of your costs agreement (cl 47(1))`

-- cl 49(2)(a) "the legal costs are reduced by 15% or more": measured against the costs as billed; exactly 15% counts
-- (fork F8).
GIVEN `the costs billed` IS A NUMBER, `the costs as adjudicated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction per cent (cl 49(2)(a))` `the costs billed` `the costs as adjudicated` MEANS
    IF `the costs billed` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN ((`the costs billed` MINUS `the costs as adjudicated`) DIVIDED BY `the costs billed`) TIMES 100
    ELSE 0

DECLARE `Adjudication costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `you, as the applicant: you applied after the Commissioner's determination under section 77N, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(4))`
    `the law practice: the costs were reduced by 15% or more, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(2)(a))`
    `the law practice: the court is satisfied it failed to comply with Part 3, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(2)(b))`
    `you, as the applicant, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(3))`
    `the law practice, as the applicant, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(3))`

GIVEN `the costs billed`                      IS A NUMBER
      `the costs as adjudicated`              IS A NUMBER
      `the court finds a Part 3 failure`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `you applied`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `after a Commissioner determination`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Adjudication costs answer`
`who pays the costs of the adjudication (cl 49)` `the costs billed` `the costs as adjudicated` `the court finds a Part 3 failure` `you applied` `after a Commissioner determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `you applied` AND `after a Commissioner determination`
            THEN `you, as the applicant: you applied after the Commissioner's determination under section 77N, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(4))`
        IF `the reduction per cent (cl 49(2)(a))` `the costs billed` `the costs as adjudicated` AT LEAST 15
            THEN `the law practice: the costs were reduced by 15% or more, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(2)(a))`
        IF `the court finds a Part 3 failure`
            THEN `the law practice: the court is satisfied it failed to comply with Part 3, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(2)(b))`
        IF `you applied`
            THEN `you, as the applicant, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(3))`
        OTHERWISE `the law practice, as the applicant, unless the court orders otherwise (cl 49(3))`
